  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.1.1: ReadRecent no longer reports a clean log it never looked at. The default budget was \"the newest 500 Application-log entries\"; on a machine with 2,351 event-1000 records in thirty days that never reached the two real crashes, so the main entry point returned zero on a machine that had crashes. It now queries the log narrowed by provider over a wall-clock window (CrashEvents.DefaultLookback, 30 days), reads each record's structured insertion strings instead of the rendered message text (the zh-CN text made the exception code come out as the faulting-module timestamp), and keeps the classic EventLog API as an explicit fallback. FaultOffset now keeps the width the log recorded (0x00000000003596cf, was 0x3596cf). 0.1.0: first publish. Event-log pairing, module version matrix, pre-crash ring buffer, Markdown report.",
